reply.Text:
No, the HIP acknowledgement is **not** an array—it's a single object. Here's the difference:

**HIP** (`POST /api/hiecm/consent/v3/request/hip/on-notify`):
```json
{
  "acknowledgement": {
    "consentId": "e3c74829-3f82-4f94-959e-e10f57bcd57b",
    "status": "OK"
  },
  "response": { "requestId": "..." }
}
```

**HIU** (`POST /api/hiecm/consent/v3/request/hiu/on-notify`):
```json
{
  "acknowledgement": [
    {
      "consentId": "e3c74829-3f82-4f94-959e-e10f57bcd57b",
      "status": "OK"
    }
  ],
  "response": { "requestId": "..." }
}
```

The HIU's `acknowledgement` is an array (can acknowledge multiple consents), while the HIP's is a single object (one acknowledgement per request). See the [HIP endpoint](https://abdm.nha.gov.in/docs/hiecm/v3/api/m2/endpoints/m2-post-consent-v3-request-hip-on-notify) and [HIU endpoint](https://abdm.nha.gov.in/docs/hiecm/v3/api/m3/endpoints/m3-post-consent-v3-request-hiu-on-notify) for details.

